<title>INDIA: Limited supply pushes up Indian soybean prices.</title>
<headline>Limited supply pushes up Indian soybean prices.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were firm in central Indian markets on limited arrivals on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said demand from processing plants was good but supply limited.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up 100 rupees per tonne on good demand and soyoil refined steady in thin trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on reports of firm trend in world markets, they said.</p>
<p>Soymeal yellow was $295-296 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in export. Rapeseed extraction was $115 per tonne FAS in export and 3,850-3,900 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition.</p>
